            <div xml:id="d34">

                <pb facs="0032" n="24" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg24"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">792.94/57: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-12T18:00:00+09:00">June 12, 1940—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 12—3:37 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>443. It was announced today at the Foreign Office that a treaty was signed at
                    Tokyo this morning with Thailand containing the following provisions: <list>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                        <item>Mutual respect for the territory of the other;</item>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                        <item>Exchange of information on matters of mutual interest;</item>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>)</label>
                        <item>Each party to refrain from assisting any nation at war with other
                            party.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
